            {
              "id": "KSV-0013",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Image tag \":latest\" used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "It is best to avoid using the ':latest' image tag when deploying containers in production. Doing so makes it hard to track which version of the image is running, and hard to roll back the version."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0013\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: Image tag \":latest\" used\nMessage: Container 'shell' of Pod 'debug' should specify an image tag\nLink: [KSV-0013](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013)\nIt is best to avoid using the ':latest' image tag when deploying containers in production. Doing so makes it hard to track which version of the image is running, and hard to roll back the version.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0013**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|MEDIUM|Image tag \":latest\" used|Container 'shell' of Pod 'debug' should specify an image tag|[KSV-0013](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013)|\n\nIt is best to avoid using the ':latest' image tag when deploying containers in production. Doing so makes it hard to track which version of the image is running, and hard to roll back the version."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
